Author: rjzaar <rjzaar@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 24 23:04:39 2026 +1000

    REVIEW(legal/cross-app): ops#118 Moodle-side Art.9 formation-data consent gate (fail-closed WORKING DRAFT)
    
    Safety partner to the nwc (Drupal) consent arc. The real special-category
    religious-formation writes happen cross-app HERE on Moodle (ssc): mod_depthcontent
    (progress/mastery/spaced-repetition/retrieval) and local_practice (practice ledger).
    Until Moodle also gates those on Art.9 consent, a no-consent (Trialing) member would
    persist special-category data on Moodle = GDPR breach. This gate carries the consent
    decision from nwc via a new OIDC claim and fails CLOSED.
    
    MUST SHIP TOGETHER with the nwc freeze-retirement / consent-arc change that EMITS the
    claim. Until then every member reads as Trialing and formation writes are skipped
    (the safe pre-rollout posture).
    
    Cross-repo contract (nwc MUST emit): userinfo boolean claim `art9_consent`
    (optional secondary `may_keep_formation`, ANDed if present).
    
    - auth_nwc\consent: pure decide() (fail-closed: null/false -> block; siteadmin -> allow)
      + Moodle I/O (store_from_userinfo / get / may_keep_formation). Carried at login as
      user pref auth_nwc_art9_consent; gate reads the STORED pref so a userinfo failure
      never opens the gate.
    - observer::user_loggedin: fetch raw userinfo ONCE, drive both guild sync (ops#93)
      and consent carry (ops#118). Missing claim on a valid userinfo -> store FALSE.
    - mod_depthcontent: gate get_progress / update_sr / apply_retrieval + early-return
      the two external write entry points (record_response, submit_review) -> ephemeral
      no-op, UX intact, nothing persisted.
    - local_practice: gate the ONE write path engaged() (returns existing false "rejected"
      contract) + set_anchor.
    - Pure unit test (plain php) for the decision truth table. version.php bumped so a
      deploy rebuilds the classmap.
    
    Tests: php -l clean on all files; consent_logic_test 6/6; live Moodle bootstrap probe
    (helper + module wrappers, admin allowed / guest+unknown blocked); functional
    write-skip proven on a throwaway user (0 rows persisted with no consent), cleaned up.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/auth/nwc/classes/consent.php b/auth/nwc/classes/consent.php
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..05942ecc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/auth/nwc/classes/consent.php
@@ -0,0 +1,217 @@
+<?php
+// This file is part of the auth_nwc plugin for Moodle (F26 nwc<->ss OIDC).
+//
+//   LEGAL / CROSS-APP SURFACE — REQUIRES HUMAN REVIEW BEFORE MERGE/ENABLE.
+//   This is the Moodle half of the ops#118 Art. 9 consent gate. It MUST ship
+//   together with the nwc (Drupal) consent-arc change that EMITS the
+//   `art9_consent` claim (see the cross-repo contract below). Until BOTH ship,
+//   this gate treats every member as Trialing (fail-closed), which is the
+//   correct pre-rollout posture but blocks real formation writes.
+//
+// GNU GPL v3 or later. Copyright 2026 Narrow Way Project.
+//
+// WHY THIS EXISTS (ops#118)
+// ------------------------
+// On nwc (Drupal) the Art. 9 formation-data freeze was retired and replaced by
+// a *capability* gate. But the REAL special-category religious-formation writes
+// happen cross-app, here on Moodle (Saint School / ssc): mod_depthcontent
+// (progress / mastery / spaced-repetition / retrieval log) and local_practice
+// (the religious PRACTICE ledger of named members). Until Moodle ALSO gates
+// those writes on Art. 9 consent, a no-consent ("Trialing") member would
+// persist special-category data on Moodle = a GDPR breach. This class carries
+// the consent decision to Moodle and is the single source of truth the two
+// modules gate their writes on.
+//
+// CROSS-REPO CONTRACT (nwc MUST emit this) — the load-bearing dependency
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+// The nwc OIDC issuer must add a boolean claim to its /oauth/userinfo response:
+//
+//     art9_consent : bool   // true  = member has given Art. 9 consent to keep
+//                           //         religious-formation data (Member tier).
+//                           // false = Trialing / consent withdrawn -> ephemeral.
+//
+// (Optional, reserved for a future finer split — NOT required by this gate:
+//     may_keep_formation : bool   // if present, ANDed with art9_consent.)
+//
+// The claim name is defined once here as self::CLAIM. auth_nwc reads it from the
+// RAW userinfo (\core\oauth2\client::get_raw_userinfo() — core drops unmapped
+// claims from get_userinfo(), exactly as for the `guilds` claim) on every login
+// and stores it as a per-user preference. The GATE itself then works purely off
+// the STORED preference, so a transient userinfo failure never silently opens
+// the gate — it just leaves the last-known (fail-closed) value in place.
+//
+// FAIL-CLOSED SEMANTICS
+// ---------------------
+//   * pref never set / unknown        -> NO consent (Trialing) -> writes skipped.
+//   * pref explicitly '0'             -> NO consent            -> writes skipped.
+//   * pref explicitly '1'             -> consent               -> writes persist.
+//   * site administrator (is_siteadmin) -> ALWAYS allowed, so CLI seeding,
+//     admin tooling and break-glass never break. Admin accounts are operators,
+//     not data subjects whose formation we are protecting.
+//   * any error evaluating the decision -> treated as NO consent.
+
+namespace auth_nwc;
+
+defined('MOODLE_INTERNAL') || die();
+
+/**
+ * Art. 9 formation-data consent state, carried nwc -> Moodle via an OIDC claim
+ * and enforced as a fail-closed write gate (ops#118).
+ *
+ * The DECISION is pure (self::decide) and unit-tested with plain PHP, matching
+ * the uid_lock / guild_cohort_map pattern. All Moodle I/O (preference read,
+ * is_siteadmin) lives in the thin self::may_keep_formation composer.
+ */
+final class consent {
+
+    /** The Moodle user-preference key that stores the carried consent state. */
+    const PREF = 'auth_nwc_art9_consent';
+
+    /** The OIDC userinfo claim nwc must emit (cross-repo contract). */
+    const CLAIM = 'art9_consent';
+
+    /**
+     * Optional secondary claim; if present it is ANDed with CLAIM. Reserved for
+     * a future finer-grained split — not required for the gate to work today.
+     */
+    const CLAIM_MAY_KEEP = 'may_keep_formation';
+
+    /**
+     * PURE decision: may we persist this member's formation data?
+     *
+     * @param bool|null $consent Stored consent tri-state: true/false, or null if
+     *                           no consent state has ever been carried/stored.
+     * @param bool      $isadmin Whether the user is a Moodle site administrator.
+     * @return bool true only when persistence is permitted; false fails closed.
+     */
+    public static function decide(?bool $consent, bool $isadmin): bool {
+        // Operators (siteadmins) are never gated: CLI seeding, admin tooling and
+        // break-glass must always work. They are not the protected data subjects.
+        if ($isadmin) {
+            return true;
+        }
+        // Fail-closed: only an explicit, carried TRUE opens the gate.
+        return $consent === true;
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Read the stored consent tri-state for a user.
+     *
+     * @param int $userid
+     * @return bool|null true='1', false='0', null=never carried/stored.
+     */
+    public static function get(int $userid): ?bool {
+        if ($userid <= 0) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        // Default sentinel distinguishes "never stored" from an explicit '0'.
+        $val = get_user_preferences(self::PREF, null, $userid);
+        if ($val === null || $val === '') {
+            return null;
+        }
+        return ((string) $val) === '1';
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Store the carried consent state for a user (called at login from the
+     * observer). Passing null CLEARS any stored value (back to fail-closed
+     * "unknown"); pass a bool to record an explicit decision.
+     *
+     * @param int       $userid
+     * @param bool|null $consent
+     * @return void
+     */
+    public static function store(int $userid, ?bool $consent): void {
+        if ($userid <= 0) {
+            return;
+        }
+        if ($consent === null) {
+            unset_user_preference(self::PREF, $userid);
+            return;
+        }
+        set_user_preference(self::PREF, $consent ? '1' : '0', $userid);
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Extract the consent decision from a RAW OIDC userinfo object and store it.
+     *
+     * Semantics (deliberately fail-closed):
+     *   * $raw is null (userinfo unreachable)        -> leave stored value alone
+     *                                                   (last-known wins; getter
+     *                                                    still fails closed if it
+     *                                                    was never set).
+     *   * CLAIM absent from an otherwise-valid $raw  -> store FALSE. nwc has not
+     *                                                   emitted the claim yet
+     *                                                   (cross-repo TODO) -> the
+     *                                                   member is Trialing.
+     *   * CLAIM present                              -> store its bool, ANDed
+     *                                                   with CLAIM_MAY_KEEP when
+     *                                                   that optional claim is set.
+     *
+     * @param int          $userid
+     * @param object|null  $raw Raw userinfo (from get_raw_userinfo()), or null.
+     * @return void
+     */
+    public static function store_from_userinfo(int $userid, ?object $raw): void {
+        if ($userid <= 0) {
+            return;
+        }
+        if ($raw === null) {
+            // Could not read userinfo this login: do NOT overwrite. Never opens
+            // the gate — the getter fails closed on a missing/last-known value.
+            return;
+        }
+        if (!isset($raw->{self::CLAIM})) {
+            // Valid userinfo but no consent claim: nwc has not implemented the
+            // contract yet. Treat as no consent (Trialing) and record it.
+            self::store($userid, false);
+            return;
+        }
+        $consent = self::truthy($raw->{self::CLAIM});
+        if ($consent && isset($raw->{self::CLAIM_MAY_KEEP})) {
+            $consent = self::truthy($raw->{self::CLAIM_MAY_KEEP});
+        }
+        self::store($userid, $consent);
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * THE gate helper. May we persist this member's formation data right now?
+     *
+     * Fail-closed by construction: any exception, missing subsystem or unknown
+     * state resolves to false. Callers in mod_depthcontent / local_practice call
+     * this immediately before an INSERT/UPDATE of per-user formation rows and
+     * SKIP the persist (silent, ephemeral no-op) when it returns false.
+     *
+     * @param int $userid
+     * @return bool
+     */
+    public static function may_keep_formation(int $userid): bool {
+        try {
+            if ($userid <= 0 || isguestuser($userid)) {
+                return false;
+            }
+            $isadmin = is_siteadmin($userid);
+            return self::decide(self::get($userid), $isadmin);
+        } catch (\Throwable $e) {
+            // Anything unexpected -> fail closed (never persist on doubt).
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Normalise a claim value that may arrive as bool, int, or string.
+     *
+     * @param mixed $v
+     * @return bool
+     */
+    private static function truthy($v): bool {
+        if (is_bool($v)) {
+            return $v;
+        }
+        if (is_int($v)) {
+            return $v === 1;
+        }
+        $s = strtolower(trim((string) $v));
+        return $s === '1' || $s === 'true' || $s === 'yes';
+    }
+}
diff --git a/auth/nwc/classes/observer.php b/auth/nwc/classes/observer.php
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..676b3d95
--- /dev/null
+++ b/auth/nwc/classes/observer.php
@@ -0,0 +1,203 @@
+<?php
+// auth_nwc observer — wires the F26 UID-lock EXECUTOR into the real post-auth
+// path for core-OAuth2 logins (fixes F26 B1: resolve_and_lock() was dead code).
+//
+//   AUTH SURFACE — REQUIRES HUMAN REVIEW BEFORE MERGE/ENABLE.
+//   UNTESTED ON MOODLE — draft for two-person review.
+//
+// GNU GPL v3 or later. Copyright 2026 Narrow Way Project.
+//
+// WHY AN EVENT OBSERVER (not user_authenticated_hook):
+//   \auth_oauth2\auth::complete_login() calls complete_user_login() DIRECTLY and
+//   deliberately bypasses authenticate_user_login() (core comment: "We used to
+//   call authenticate_user - but that won't work if the current user has a
+//   different default authentication type."). authenticate_user_login() is the
+//   ONLY caller of auth_plugin_base::user_authenticated_hook(), so that hook never
+//   fires on the OAuth2 path. \core\event\user_loggedin DOES fire (from
+//   complete_user_login()) for every successful login regardless of auth path.
+//
+// LIMITATION (flagged for the 2-person review):
+//   This observer runs AFTER core has already created/linked and logged the user
+//   in. It enforces the lock as a GUARD + REPAIR (assert idnumber==sub; DENY and
+//   kill the session on a broken/empty sub). It does NOT pre-empt core's own
+//   email-based linking. The durable happy-path lock remains the REQUIRED issuer
+//   field-mapping sub->idnumber (INSTALL.md §2): core writes idnumber at account
+//   creation and never rewrites it. Faithfully running the migration LOCK_EXISTING
+//   branch (needs mid-flow email_verified + the pre-link row) or the SUSPEND branch
+//   (needs a live userinfo probe) requires, respectively, owning the callback and a
+//   scheduled reconcile task — see TODO(build-host) markers below.
+
+namespace auth_nwc;
+
+defined('MOODLE_INTERNAL') || die();
+
+class observer {
+
+    /**
+     * Runs on every successful login; acts only for logins through OUR nwc issuer.
+     *
+     * @param \core\event\user_loggedin $event
+     */
+    public static function user_loggedin(\core\event\user_loggedin $event): void {
+        global $DB;
+
+        $config = get_config('auth_nwc');
+
+        // 0. Do nothing unless the plugin is enabled AND pointed at an issuer.
+        //    Enabling/disabling auth_nwc is the operator's on/off switch for
+        //    lock ENFORCEMENT (core still uses authtype 'oauth2' for the dance).
+        if (empty($config->issuerid) || !is_enabled_auth('nwc')) {
+            return;
+        }
+
+        $userid = (int) ($event->objectid ?? $event->userid);
+        if (empty($userid)) {
+            return;
+        }
+        $user = $DB->get_record('user', ['id' => $userid]);
+        if (!$user) {
+            return;
+        }
+
+        // 1. GUARD: only touch logins that actually came through our nwc issuer.
+        //    Core stamps auth='oauth2' (not 'nwc') and owns the linked-login row
+        //    keyed by issuerid — that row is the reliable "this was our SSO" signal.
+        //    TODO(build-host): confirm the linked_login row already exists when
+        //    user_loggedin fires (it is created earlier, inside complete_login()).
+        $islinked = $DB->record_exists('auth_oauth2_linked_login', [
+            'userid'   => $user->id,
+            'issuerid' => (int) $config->issuerid,
+        ]);
+        if (!$islinked) {
+            return; // manual / admin / other-issuer login — not ours.
+        }
+
+        // 2. Obtain the nwc uid (`sub`). Core wrote it to mdl_user.idnumber via the
+        //    REQUIRED issuer field-mapping sub->idnumber at account creation, and
+        //    does not rewrite it on later logins — so that mapped value IS the sub.
+        //    TODO(build-host): if sub is ALSO mapped to username, corroborate
+        //    $user->idnumber against auth_oauth2_linked_login.username here.
+        //    TODO(build-host): if idnumber is empty, the mapping is not configured
+        //    -> decision is DENY -> ALL logins are rejected. Verify the mapping is
+        //    in place BEFORE enabling auth_nwc.
+        $claims = [
+            'sub'            => (string) $user->idnumber,
+            'email'          => $user->email,
+            // email_verified is asserted by the issuer MID-FLOW and is not available
+            // at this post-login event; we pass false so the observer never performs
+            // an email-based re-link. The migration LOCK_EXISTING branch is therefore
+            // out of scope for the observer — see LIMITATION above.
+            'email_verified' => false,
+            'given_name'     => $user->firstname,
+            'family_name'    => $user->lastname,
+        ];
+
+        // 3. At a successful login the nwc account, by definition, just resolved,
+        //    so nwc_active=true here. The SUSPEND-on-nwc-deletion branch needs a
+        //    LIVE userinfo probe and belongs in a scheduled reconcile task, NOT the
+        //    login hook. TODO(build-host): add \auth_nwc\task\reconcile_locks
+        //    (db/tasks.php) to walk locked rows, call userinfo, and SUSPEND rows
+        //    whose nwc account is gone (uid_lock already returns ACTION_SUSPEND).
+        $nwcactive = true;
+
+        // 4. Run the pure, unit-tested decision + its $DB executor.
+        $auth = get_auth_plugin('nwc'); // auth_plugin_nwc
+        $decision = $auth->resolve_and_lock($claims, $nwcactive);
+
+        // 5. SESSION-level enforcement (resolve_and_lock only mutates $DB rows).
+        switch ($decision['action']) {
+            case uid_lock::ACTION_DENY:
+            case uid_lock::ACTION_SUSPEND:
+                // Broken/empty sub, or a lock that must not stand: tear the session
+                // down and bounce to the login page with a neutral error.
+                // TODO(build-host): review UX + whether redirect() from inside an
+                //   observer is acceptable on your Moodle version (observers run
+                //   synchronously within complete_user_login()); an alternative is
+                //   to set a session flag and redirect at the next require_login().
+                \core\session\manager::kill_user_sessions($user->id);
+                if (!during_initial_install() && !CLI_SCRIPT) {
+                    redirect(new \moodle_url('/login/index.php'),
+                        get_string('locked_denied', 'auth_nwc'), null,
+                        \core\output\notification::NOTIFY_ERROR);
+                }
+                break;
+
+            case uid_lock::ACTION_REUSE_LOCKED:
+            case uid_lock::ACTION_LOCK_EXISTING:
+            case uid_lock::ACTION_CREATE:
+            default:
+                // Happy path: the lock is intact / was just (re)applied by the
+                // executor. Read the nwc userinfo ONCE and drive both claim-pull
+                // reconciliations off it. Best-effort throughout: any failure is
+                // swallowed so it can never break a login.
+                $raw = self::fetch_raw_userinfo($config, $user);
+
+                // (ops#118) Carry the Art. 9 consent state into Moodle so the
+                // formation-write gate can enforce it. A null $raw (userinfo
+                // unreachable) deliberately leaves the last-known value in place
+                // — store_from_userinfo() never opens the gate on a bad fetch.
+                \auth_nwc\consent::store_from_userinfo((int) $user->id, $raw);
+
+                // (ops#93) Reconcile guild cohorts from the `guilds` claim.
+                $guilds = self::guilds_from_userinfo($raw);
+                if ($guilds !== null) {
+                    $auth->sync_guilds((int) $user->id, $guilds);
+                }
+                break;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Fetch the FULL raw nwc userinfo object from the OIDC userinfo endpoint.
+     *
+     * Neither the `guilds` nor the ops#118 `art9_consent` claim is written to any
+     * mdl_user field, so both must be read from userinfo. Core's get_userinfo()
+     * drops unmapped claims, so we use get_raw_userinfo(), which carries the full
+     * claim set. The user-tier access token is in the session (core stored it
+     * during complete_login, which runs in this same request), so no re-auth is
+     * needed.
+     *
+     * Returns the raw userinfo object, or null if it could not be obtained (a
+     * later reconcile task with no live session token also gets null — a
+     * scheduled userinfo probe is the right place for that path).
+     *
+     * @param \stdClass $config auth_nwc config (has issuerid).
+     * @param \stdClass $user   The Moodle user.
+     * @return object|null
+     */
+    protected static function fetch_raw_userinfo(\stdClass $config, \stdClass $user): ?object {
+        try {
+            $issuer = \core\oauth2\api::get_issuer((int) $config->issuerid);
+            if (!$issuer || !$issuer->get('enabled')) {
+                return null;
+            }
+            $client = \core\oauth2\api::get_user_oauth_client(
+                $issuer, new \moodle_url('/auth/oauth2/login.php'));
+            if (!$client || !$client->is_logged_in()) {
+                return null;
+            }
+            $raw = $client->get_raw_userinfo();
+            return is_object($raw) ? $raw : null;
+        } catch (\Throwable $e) {
+            return null;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Extract the `guilds` claim from a raw userinfo object (pure, no I/O).
+     *
+     * Returns the normalised guilds array, or null if the claim is absent/ill-
+     * formed. Null means "leave cohorts alone" — the caller never strips managed
+     * cohorts on a missing claim (returning [] would remove all; too destructive).
+     *
+     * @param object|null $raw
+     * @return array|null
+     */
+    protected static function guilds_from_userinfo(?object $raw): ?array {
+        if (!is_object($raw) || !isset($raw->guilds) || !is_array($raw->guilds)) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        // Normalise stdClass entries to arrays for the pure decider.
+        return array_map(fn($g) => (array) $g, $raw->guilds);
+    }
+}
diff --git a/auth/nwc/tests/consent_logic_test.php b/auth/nwc/tests/consent_logic_test.php
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..f75bdb1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/auth/nwc/tests/consent_logic_test.php
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+<?php
+// Standalone unit test for auth_nwc\consent::decide — runs with plain `php`,
+// no Moodle. Verifies the fail-closed ops#118 Art. 9 gate decision.
+//
+//   php auth/nwc/tests/consent_logic_test.php
+//
+// The Moodle I/O half (preference read, is_siteadmin, claim extraction) lives in
+// consent::may_keep_formation / store_from_userinfo and needs a Moodle test env;
+// the load-bearing DECISION is pure and covered here.
+
+// consent.php calls defined('MOODLE_INTERNAL') || die(); satisfy it for standalone run.
+define('MOODLE_INTERNAL', true);
+require __DIR__ . '/../classes/consent.php';
+
+use auth_nwc\consent;
+
+$pass = 0; $fail = 0;
+function check($name, $got, $want) {
+    global $pass, $fail;
+    $g = var_export($got, true);
+    $w = var_export($want, true);
+    if ($got === $want) { echo "  ok   $name\n"; $pass++; }
+    else { echo "  FAIL $name (got $g, want $w)\n"; $fail++; }
+}
+
+// --- decide(): fail-closed truth table -------------------------------------
+
+// 1. Explicit consent + ordinary member -> allowed.
+check('consent=true, member -> keep', consent::decide(true, false), true);
+
+// 2. Explicit NO consent + ordinary member -> blocked (fail closed).
+check('consent=false, member -> block', consent::decide(false, false), false);
+
+// 3. Unknown / never-carried + ordinary member -> blocked (fail closed).
+check('consent=null, member -> block', consent::decide(null, false), false);
+
+// 4. Site admin is NEVER gated, regardless of stored consent.
+check('admin overrides null', consent::decide(null, true), true);
+check('admin overrides false', consent::decide(false, true), true);
+check('admin with consent', consent::decide(true, true), true);
+
+echo "== $pass passed, $fail failed ==\n";
+exit($fail === 0 ? 0 : 1);
